        <type>uint64_t</type>
        <definition>uint64_t MemoryInFiles::Impl::MemoryBlockInfo::Resize</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::shared_ptr&lt; FileInfo &gt; &amp;currentFileInfoPtr, const uint64_t currentBaseOffsetWithinFile, const uint64_t newLengthAlignedToBlockSize)</argsstring>
        <name>Resize</name>
        <param>
          <type>const std::shared_ptr&lt; <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1FileInfo" kindref="compound">FileInfo</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>currentFileInfoPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint64_t</type>
          <declname>currentBaseOffsetWithinFile</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint64_t</type>
          <declname>newLengthAlignedToBlockSize</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Resize this memory block. If new length is smaller than the current length, returns immediately with a value of 0. Else, on the current active write file creates a new fragment that covers the length difference, thus expanding this memory block by the desired amount. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>currentFileInfoPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The current active write file. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>currentBaseOffsetWithinFile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The current active file offset to begin writing from. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>newLengthAlignedToBlockSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The target memory block length in bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The increase in size (NOT the total size of the new allocation) if resizing to a larger length, or 0 if the new length is smaller than the current length. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
