      <memberdef kind="function" id="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1MemoryBlockInfo_1a0681ebaeac8aab90fc01f7f7cc58c3e2" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool MemoryInFiles::Impl::MemoryBlockInfo::DoWriteOrRead</definition>
        <argsstring>(const uint64_t deferredOffset, const uint64_t deferredLength, void *readToThisLocationPtr, const void *writeFromThisLocationPtr, void *handlerPtrPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>DoWriteOrRead</name>
        <param>
          <type>const uint64_t</type>
          <declname>deferredOffset</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint64_t</type>
          <declname>deferredLength</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>readToThisLocationPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const void *</type>
          <declname>writeFromThisLocationPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>handlerPtrPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Initiate a read or write operation. If the block is due deletion or the data length to operate on exceeds the allocated size of the block, returns immediately. Else, acts accordingly to the following cases:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>When (readToThisLocationPtr == NULL), we are attempting to queue a write operation, calls <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1FileInfo_1ac907aae793c0e7e2c3d4ffd82efab539" kindref="member">FileInfo::WriteMemoryAsync()</ref> on each eligible fragment.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>When (writeFromThisLocationPtr == NULL), we are attempting to queue a read operation, calls <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1FileInfo_1ab25a82cecb4f7a0dc70f181264e2a1bf" kindref="member">FileInfo::ReadMemoryAsync()</ref> on each eligible fragment. Eligible is any fragment that overlaps with the range we are operating on [deferredOffset, (deferredOffset + deferredLength)], as such if N fragments are eligible, this function will queue N individual I/O operations. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deferredOffset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The target memory block offset. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deferredLength</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The data length in bytes to read or write. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>readToThisLocationPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type-erased output begin pointer in case of read, NULL on write. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>writeFromThisLocationPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type-erased input begin pointer in case of write, NULL on read. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handlerPtrPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type-erased I/O completion handler pointer. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the operation could be queued successfully, or False otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
